{"text": "ADSORPTION OF NICOTINE UNDER VARIOUS CONDITIONS\n\nH. Schievetbein\n\nT am very honoured to be invited to speak for this gathering\nof distinguished experts on nicotine metabolism and estimation.\nAs I am the only invited participant whose native tongue is\nnot English I would like to announce that-any remark that I\nwill make that is not in accordance with the opinion of this\nmeeting is only due to my inabitity to express myself correctly\nin English.\n\nThe position of the first speaker is somewhat precarious as\nhe does not know what cones after him. I have decided to give\n2 conference warming lecture, that is, I would Tike to discuss\nsome points which may contribute to later discussions and the\noutcome of this conference. 1 am aware of the fact that the\nexperimental work I will talk about is known to you, but I\nhave put them together so that they may be of value for our\ndiscussions on the importance of nicotine absorption under\nsmoking conditions. First I will make some general remarks\nwith regards to tobacco consumption, then sone historical re-\nmarks on nicotine estimation and at the end I will present to\nyou the results of our own experiments.\n\nIn 1974 in Beitrage zur Tabakforschung Misfield and Timm had\npublished a paper on statistical measurements of tobacco con-\nsumption in West Germany. They reported (Fi 1) a gradually\nrise in cigarette consumption during the years 1961-73. The\n\n501602018",
